POLE: violation. Expected judge answer: compliant = false, naming at least one breach.

Breaches present, any one of which is sufficient:

- rule-authoring MUST-1: the primary modal in both clauses is "should" /
  "where practical" / "generally", so neither clause states an obligation. The
  headings advertise MUST Rules over hedged bodies.
- The DO and DO-NOT halves of both code blocks are BYTE-IDENTICAL, so the
  contrast teaches nothing.
- The BLOCKED corpora are abstract exhortations ("do not be careless"), not
  rationalizations an agent would actually produce, so nothing is recognizable
  at the moment of the decision.
- Each **Why:** restates the clause instead of naming a consequence.
- hook-output-discipline MUST-2: the Wiring block assigns "block" severity at
  the hook layer on an explicitly LEXICAL scan.
- coc-artifact-eval-coverage MUST-4 / verification-gate-integrity MUST-1: the
  Detection field claims a scanner, a fixture directory and a probe suite that
  are all wired and green, and asserts no gate-review is owed. None of the three
  cited paths exists.
- Origin cites no measurement and no date — "general experience" and "the
  accumulated view of the authors".

A judge must NOT clear this because the eight Wiring fields are present and
ordered: they are required to be ACCURATE, not merely present.

